  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening quality capabilities for compliance with standards in Colombian micro-, small and medium-sized enterprises. Quality training and extension programme for micro-, small and medium-sized en</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia is in the early stages of implementing its Reindustrialization Policy, aligned with the 2022#2026 National Development Plan, to strengthen regional business networks, reduce productivity gaps, and promote a more inclusive and competitive economy. MSMEs#representing 99.5% of the business fabric, generating 79% of employment, and contributing up to 40% of GDP#are central to this effort but continue to face structural barriers that limit their competitiveness and productivity, including marginal access to international markets and low compliance with technical norms and quality standards. This project addresses these challenges by seeking to close structural and quality gaps in MSMEs within prioritized sectors through capacity building, targeted technical support, and the promotion of effective use of quality infrastructure. In doing so, it aims to enhance MSME participation in global value chains and expand their access to both local and international markets.</narrative>
  </description>
